          "note": "Prefixes: a main subheading of 1.2 International System of Units, its own page (owner 2026-11-04); PDF 5-5."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Most prefixes indicate order of magnitude in steps of 1000 and provide a convenient way to express large and small numbers, to eliminate non-significant digits. SI also includes four of the other prefixes to accommodate usage already established before the introduction of SI (Table 1.3). They are centi-(10⁻²), deci-(10⁻¹), deka-(10¹) and hecto-(10²)."
